data: {"type":"text","text":"**\"Not proven yet\" means the data lean toward warming, but the test doesn't pass our cutoff.** This is for yearly average air temperature (T2M), 2000–2020, 21 years each.\n\n- **Belgium:** The Sen slope is 0.44 °C per decade. The Mann-Kendall p-value is 0.043, but the adjusted OLS p-value is 0.079. The verdict uses the larger p-value, and that is above 0.05. The two tests disagree.\n- **Netherlands:** The Sen slope is 0.35 °C per decade. The Mann-Kendall p-value is 0.065 and the OLS p-value is 0.198. Both are above 0.05.\n- **Extra years:** If the slope and noise stay the same, roughly 2 more years for Belgium and 7 for the Netherlands might get these over the line. That is approximate and not guaranteed.\n- **Limits:** The p-values are nominal and depend on the test's assumptions. \"Not proven yet\" does not mean \"no change\". Belgium's data also used a nearest-cell fallback."}

